{"contract":"translation_contextual_v2","candidate_identity":"8f6d70f76e70fab512caffce6e8f578a6e3546bb6009fa88a609529f7493cb25","verdicts":[{"revision_key":"ff891672cbe466bfc528600f8cd25b7b9180949d59679f1178836e0102392f44","verdict":"ISSUE","observation":"The source name is \"Sceptre of the Archlich\" (world-artifacts.lua:2637, define_as SET_SCEPTRE_LICH at @624a673). The target \"死灵权杖\" (\"necromantic sceptre\") drops the named owner \"Archlich\" (大巫妖), so the unique artifact's name no longer marks its link to the archlich/lich set. The frozen terminology has no entry for Archlich, so this relies on the source text only. Suggested wording: \"大巫妖权杖\" or similar."},{"revision_key":"ffa77aef82eb16f84cf30296ac11291883baae8a494cbb97b9b5a686459bb60f","verdict":"OK"},{"revision_key":"ffb21dd4ccd3ada3cb0abcecd6ee531904750bce1b6d8b41fdc441b29cf91839","verdict":"ISSUE","observation":"magical.lua:608/634 @624a673: this message is shown when Supercharge or Overload ends, and it pairs with \"#Target# is overloaded with power.\" The effect it removes is inc_damage (all=25 or power). The source \"seems less dangerous\" means the target now looks less threatening because it lost the damage boost. The target \"平静了下来\" (\"has calmed down\") changes this into an emotional or state calming and loses the meaning of reduced threat. Suggested wording: \"看起来没那么危险了\"."},{"revision_key":"ffd4751c6be1cc762e0917b44dbb91251580eeee3caa072dc64b9ba51cfe5068","verdict":"OK"},{"revision_key":"ffe80f4c81073264933cfb717896ef7ecf7004171e9a9030e065ac3dab3101ae","verdict":"ISSUE","observation":"portal-vault.lua:133 @624a673: the source \"A strange portal to some place else.\" contains the qualifier \"strange\". The target \"通向其他地方的传送门。\" leaves out \"奇怪的／奇异的\" (\"strange\"), so part of the description is missing. Suggested wording: \"一道通往别处的奇异传送门。\""},{"revision_key":"fff8487389cbed3c2897bfc85f6d3c264537cae71a0985cdbf5e67c64a34c076","verdict":"ISSUE","observation":"The source says \"Stone golems are formidable foes that can become unstoppable.\" In summon-melee.lua @624a673, the summoned golem gets resolvers.talents{[Talents.T_UNSTOPPABLE]=3,...} (about line 504). It becomes unstoppable by using the Unstoppable talent, not permanently. The target \"并且不可阻挡\" (\"and are unstoppable\") drops the modal \"can become\" and states the effect as permanent, which is a mechanical error. Suggested wording: \"可以变得不可阻挡\"."}]}